{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1391490-victorian-age-brujah-bloodline-the-aigles","id":1391490,"title":"[Victorian Age] Brujah Bloodline: The Aigles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-25T09:24:45-07:00","id":1391490,"title":"[Victorian Age] Brujah Bloodline: The Aigles","content":"Found some extra time on my hands so I made this write up as I've been reading and listning a little about the Napoleonic Era. I think personally that the French Revolution and the First French Empire is a pretty good source of inspriation for older Brujah who wants to change the Camarilla dramatically but not necessarily out of belief in egalitarianism in a modern sense.<br /> <br /> Also I tried to keep the text short so that it would be readable and not a wall of text that no one will read.<br /> <br /> <b>Name: </b>Aigle<br /> <br /> <br /> Born in blood and fear and letting them pull their chariot, the Aigle came into being in the tumult of the French Revolution and blossomed with the First French Empire. In the early years of the Bloodline such a figure emerged among the Damned to fight the stagnated rule inside the Camarilla and gathered the Parisian Kindred to its colour and in a frenzied orgy they fought as the human revolutionaries were seized by the same frenzy, both against the old order for something new. In the end the Bloodline was driven out of Paris after its leader, a mysterious figure only, known as the Eagle, went down fighting. Chased off but not defeated, the Bloodline spread its revolutionary zeal and in the absence of its former leader lionized Napoleon, Emperor of France, as their great hero.<br /> <br /> Like many other Brujah the Aigles strive for enlightenment, an end to the old corrupt order and the rise of a new vigorous one. They can see how many of their ideas are picking up speed and that it won\u2019t be long before a new Napoleon rises to shake the foundations of the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Eagles<br /> <br /> <b>Sect:</b> Mixed, mostly Camarilla and some Anarchs. Many are part of the Camarilla which they wish to take over and reshape into something new and vigorous and throw the conservative order to the guillotine of enlightenment.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Well-groomed and often with a certain military streak to them. Be it a medal from their mortal days or a weapon or so.<br /> <br /> <b>Havens:</b> Often expensive and well-kept, many keep some form of cameo or keepsake connected with Napoleon and the French Empire.<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Aigles are most recruited from the middle class and there is certain class contempt among them against both the degenerated upper class and the servile lower classes. Eagles tend to be of a socially progressive bent but often with an impatience to re-fashion the world to a socially, if not politically, better place.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Creation:</b> Social and Physical attributes are at the top and many have either some kind of martial background or become enamoured with the idea of spreading progressive values at the point of a rifle under the tutorship of their sires.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Celerity, Fortitude, Dominate<br /> <br /> W<b>eakness:</b> Test for Frenzy at a -3 penalty when seeing what they can identify as Vitae, or tasting or smelling Vitae themselves. The archaic servitude of the blood bound is anathema to the Aigles and they react violently to any hint of it.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization: </b>The Eagles are curiously not very well organized and since the disgrace of Napoleon III the bloodline has been grasping for a way forward. While they can be locally well-organized, the bloodline has little to no overarching organization after a great surge under the Second French Empire.<br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> \u201cWe will shake the foundations of your world.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes</b><br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue, Toreador and Tremere:</b> The guardians of corruption who will soon have their world torn asunder in a storm the like of which will never be forgotten.<br /> <br /> <b>Gangrel, Malkavians and Nosferatu</b>: Keep an eye on them. Their rage and despair can be useful but will need to be kept from diverging the proper path of our revolution.<br /> <br /> <b>Camarilla: </b>The vehicle of oppression which we will turn into our weapon of liberation.<br /> <br /> <b>Sabbat: </b>Rabble is rabble.<br /> ..<br /> <b>Anarchs: </b>...is rabble","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}